{
  "uid": "sli-slo",
  "title": "SLO, error budget, and traffic",
  "description": "Availability and latency SLOs for the sample service, the 30-day error budgets, multi-window burn rates, and the RED charts that explain a burn.",
  "tags": [
    "slo"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "15s",
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "SLO",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Availability.** 99.5% of valid requests return 2xx, over 30 days. Valid means 2xx or 5xx. A 4xx is outside the SLI.\n\n**Latency.** 99% of successful requests finish in 300 ms or less, over 30 days. The SLI is the 300 ms histogram bucket, not a percentile.\n\n**Paging.** Burn above 14.4 on both 5m and 1h, or above 6 on both 30m and 6h. The 3x / 1 day and 1x / 3 day burns open a ticket. There is no CPU alert.\n\nThe budget is a share of the allowance, not a slice of the month. 100% means the allowed failures are all still unused. 0% means they are used up. Below 0%, each extra -100% is one more budget the requests so far have cost. A few minutes of almost-all 500s on a young stand is many budgets, because almost every request failed and almost none were allowed. The 3.6 hours only describe a month where every minute has the same traffic."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Availability",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Availability, 30d",
      "description": "Share of valid requests (2xx or 5xx) that returned 2xx. A 4xx is excluded.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 2,
          "noValue": "no traffic",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.99
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.995
              }
            ]
          }
        }
